# Template for the gitignored `.env` — the single local secrets file.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the DEV Supabase project's values (halcyon-dev).
#
# Who reads `.env`:
#   1. Docker Compose — interpolates ${...} in compose.yaml from it (Compose only
#      reads a file literally named `.env`), forwarding NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#      + SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY into the app container.
#   2. Next.js — its lowest-precedence env file; how the browser/SSR clients get
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY.
#
# What does NOT go here:
#   - DATABASE_URL / DIRECT_URL — never. Local Postgres URLs come from
#     compose.yaml (container) and .env.development (host `pnpm dev`).
#     Production URLs live only in Vercel env vars and CI secrets, so no local
#     file can point tooling at the production database.
#   - Production Supabase keys — production config lives in Vercel.
#
# All three vars are validated at server startup (src/lib/env.ts via
# src/instrumentation.ts); a missing value fails the boot with a clear error.
# The mail vars at the bottom are the exception — they are optional.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where every variable is set, per environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | Variable                             | What / why                               | Required | Production            | Local                 | CI / e2e              |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL             | Supabase project URL. Public by design;  | yes      | Vercel                | `.env` (halcyon-dev)  | playwright.config.ts  |
# |                                      | inlined into the browser bundle.         |          |                       |                       | (mock auth server)    |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY | Browser/SSR auth key. Public by design;  | yes      | Vercel                | `.env` (halcyon-dev)  | playwright.config.ts  |
# |                                      | RLS gates what it can do.                |          |                       |                       | (dummy)               |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY                  | Server-only admin key; bypasses RLS.     | yes      | Vercel                | `.env` (halcyon-dev)  | playwright.config.ts  |
# |                                      | Account deletion + seed demo user.       |          |                       |                       | (dummy)               |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | DATABASE_URL                         | The app's Prisma connection. Never in    | yes      | Vercel                | `.env.development`    | ci.yml job env;       |
# | (pooled, port 6543 in prod)          | `.env`, so no local file can reach prod. |          |                       | (host), compose.yaml  | test:integration      |
# |                                      |                                          |          |                       | (container)           | script                |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | DIRECT_URL                           | Only `prisma migrate` reads it (the      | migrate  | GitHub secret         | compose.yaml only     | derived in ci.yml     |
# | (direct, port 5432 in prod)          | pooler can't migrate). Prod migrations   | only     | PROD_DIRECT_URL       | (unset on host: stray | steps                 |
# |                                      | run in CI, so it's a GitHub secret, not  |          |                       | migrate fails)        |                       |
# |                                      | Vercel.                                  |          |                       |                       |                       |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | RESEND_API_KEY                       | Sends the monthly reminder email. Unset  | no       | Vercel                | unset                 | unset                 |
# |                                      | = no email sent.                         |          |                       |                       |                       |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | EMAIL_FROM                           | Reminder sender; must be on a Resend-    | no       | Vercel                | unset                 | unset                 |
# |                                      | verified domain.                         |          |                       |                       |                       |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | SITE_URL                             | Absolute origin for links in emails; a   | no       | Vercel                | unset                 | unset                 |
# |                                      | cron job has no request to derive it     |          |                       |                       |                       |
# |                                      | from.                                    |          |                       |                       |                       |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | CRON_SECRET                          | Bearer Vercel sends to cron routes;      | no       | Vercel AND GitHub     | unset                 | unset                 |
# |                                      | GitHub's copy lets health.yml /          |          | secret (must match)   |                       |                       |
# |                                      | smoke.yml call /api/health. Mismatch =   |          |                       |                       |                       |
# |                                      | 401.                                     |          |                       |                       |                       |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL               | Rate limiter store (sign-in/sign-up).    | no       | Vercel                | unset                 | unset                 |
# |                                      | Unset = limiter no-ops.                  |          |                       |                       |                       |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
# | UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN             | Rate limiter auth token, paired with the | no       | Vercel                | unset                 | unset                 |
# |                                      | URL above.                               |          |                       |                       |                       |
# +--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------+----------+-----------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------+
#
# Notes:
#   - Vercel holds all production app config; nothing in prod reads a file.
#   - Set GitHub secrets interactively (`gh secret set NAME`, then paste); piped
#     from a non-TTY, gh stores an empty value.
#
# Not env vars, but config the app depends on — Supabase dashboard:
#   - Auth → URL Configuration: Site URL + redirect allow-list. The app sends
#     ${origin}/auth/callback, so every serving origin must be listed.
#   - Auth → Providers → Google: the OAuth client ID/secret live here, not in
#     the app — Supabase performs the exchange.
#   - Settings → API Keys: source of the three Supabase values above.
# Resend issues RESEND_API_KEY (its DNS records live in Vercel DNS); Upstash
# issues the two UPSTASH_* values.
#
# Test/tooling vars (never in prod, never in .env — each has a default or is
# supplied by what runs it): CI, E2E_DATABASE_URL, PLAYWRIGHT_*,
# MOCK_SUPABASE_PORT, SMOKE_BASE_URL, ALLOW_MIXED_SCHEMA, CAPTURE_*.

# Project URL and publishable key — safe to expose to the browser; RLS gates
# what the publishable key can do. Dashboard: halcyon-dev → Settings → API Keys.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://DEV_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_…

# Server-only secret key (bypasses RLS) — used by the admin client
# (deleteMyAccount) and the seed's demo-user creation. Never expose with a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Dashboard: halcyon-dev → Settings → API Keys → Secret keys.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_…

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Monthly reminder email — ALL OPTIONAL.
#
# Leave these unset and nothing breaks: the cron route reports "email not
# configured" and sends nothing, which is what local dev, CI and preview
# deploys all do. They are set in Vercel's production environment only.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY   resend.com → API Keys. Sending-only permission is enough.
# EMAIL_FROM       must be an address on a domain verified in Resend (SPF +
#                  DKIM records on balanced.money), or delivery fails.
# SITE_URL         absolute origin for links in the email. There is no request
#                  to derive it from inside a cron job.
# CRON_SECRET      Vercel sends this as `Authorization: Bearer <value>` on
#                  scheduled invocations. Without it the cron route returns 401
#                  and sends nothing — it refuses rather than standing open.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_…
# EMAIL_FROM=Balanced Money <reminders@balanced.money>
# SITE_URL=https://balanced.money
# CRON_SECRET=example-secret

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App-side rate limiter (sign-in / sign-up) — BOTH OPTIONAL.
#
# Leave unset and the limiter no-ops (local dev, CI, preview). Set in Vercel's
# production environment to bound brute-force and confirmation-email spam by
# real client IP. A managed Upstash Redis; both values from the Upstash console.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://EXAMPLE.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=example-token
